.Dd January 25, 2026
.Dt DEVICE_CREATE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm device_create
.Nd allocate and initialize a new device structure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Ft struct device *
.Fn device_create "const char *name" "struct device *parent"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn device_create
function allocates memory for a new
.Vt struct device
and initializes it.
.Pp
If
.Fa parent
is not NULL, the new device is added to the parent's children list.
.Pp
The reference count of the new device is initialized to 1.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn device_create
function returns a pointer to the new device on success, or
.Dv NULL
if memory allocation fails.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr device 9 ,
.Xr device_register 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn device_create
kernel interface first appeared in Substrate.
